// Content for the programmatic SEO pages. Every claim here must match how DefyShare
// actually works:
//   - Files are uploaded over HTTPS to temporary cloud storage (Backblaze B2) and listed
//     through Supabase. Transfers are NOT peer-to-peer and DO pass through servers.
//   - Devices on the same Wi-Fi (same public IP address) join the same room automatically.
//   - No account is needed. Everything shared is deleted automatically after 3 hours.
//   - Each file can be up to 30 MB (paid plans are switched off in features.ts).
// Keep this file free of path aliases and non-erasable TS syntax: Node runs it directly.

/** Per-file upload limit on the free plan. */
export const FILE_LIMIT = '30 MB';
/** How long shared files and text stay before they are deleted. */
export const RETENTION = '3 hours';

/** One-paragraph, accurate explanation of how a transfer works. Used by several templates. */
export const HOW_IT_WORKS =
  `When you drop a file, your browser uploads it over HTTPS to temporary cloud storage. Every device in your room — the devices on the same Wi-Fi, which join automatically — sees it in the list and can download it. After ${RETENTION} the file is deleted for good.`;

